# Error Handling

- Never swallow errors; handle them where you can act, otherwise propagate with context.
- Distinguish expected failures (validation, not found) from bugs; return the former, throw/panic for the latter.
- Add timeouts and bounded retries (with backoff and jitter) only for idempotent operations.
- Log once, at the boundary, with structured context and no secrets.
- Show users actionable messages; keep stack traces for logs.
